# Cache-Control rules. This deploys as a static-assets Worker, not Pages,
# but the _headers file works the same way and is picked up from the repo root.
# https://developers.cloudflare.com/workers/static-assets/headers/
#
# HTML pages stay short-lived so edits (new cases, copy fixes) show up quickly.
#
# Assets are cached for a year and marked immutable, which is only safe because
# every asset URL carries a hand-bumped ?v=N (see the <link>/<script> tags in
# index.html and the game pages). That version token lives in the HTML, so it
# ships on the HTML's 300s TTL — bump it in the same commit as an asset change
# and every visitor picks up both within five minutes.
#
# Without the token this was a real bug, not just staleness: HTML expires after
# 300s but assets sat in the browser cache for 24h, so a returning visitor could
# pair NEW html with an OLD game-engine.js. Add a question type and the stale
# engine renders the prompt with no answer UI at all (buildInteractiveBody has
# no else branch); add an engine helper and the page throws and #app stays
# blank. Both are silent — no error, nothing in the console.
#
# Fonts under /assets/fonts/ deliberately carry NO ?v= (their preload href must
# match base.css's url() exactly). They are immutable by filename instead —
# see assets/fonts/LICENSE.md.

/
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=300, must-revalidate

/index.html
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=300, must-revalidate

/games/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=300, must-revalidate

/assets/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable
